      "question_id": "mathematics_undergraduate_doc_03_mathematics_long_2",
      "question_type": "LONG",
      "stem_text": "A function $f$ is defined by $f(z) = i\\overline{z}$, where $i^2 = -1$ and $\\overline{z}$\nis the complex conjugate of $z$. How many values of $z$ satisfy both $|z| = 5$ and $f(z) =\nz$?",
      "options": null,
      "marks": 10,
      "gold_answer": "Let $z = x + yi,$ where $x$ and $y$ are real numbers. Then $|z| = 5$ becomes $x^2 + y^2 =\n25,$ and $f(z) = z$ becomes \\[i(x - yi) = x + yi.\\]Then $ix + y = x + yi,$ so $x = y.$\nHence, $2x^2 = 25,$ which has two solutions. Thus, there are $\\boxed{2}$ such values of\n$z.$",
